{"title":"The English Lakes","author":"W. T. Palmer","gender":"M","genre":"Guide","year":1900,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/57664/pg57664.txt","reason":"Victorian walking guide covering major Lake District valleys and peaks."}
{"title":"Lays and Legends of the English Lake Country","author":"John Pagen White","gender":"M","genre":"Poetry","year":1873,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/48207/pg48207.txt","reason":"A collection of folk tales and poetic legends set in the Cumberland and Westmorland mountains."}
{"title":"Rock-climbing in the English Lake District","author":"Owen Glynne Jones","gender":"M","genre":"Mountaineering","year":1897,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/56043/pg56043.txt","reason":"Foundational text for early rock climbing focused entirely on the crags of the Lake District."}
{"title":"Bygone Cumberland and Westmorland","author":"Daniel Scott","gender":"M","genre":"History","year":1899,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/37891/pg37891.txt","reason":"Detailed antiquarian history of the Lake District counties, covering customs, laws, and topography."}
{"title":"The Collected Writings of Thomas De Quincey, Vol. II","author":"Thomas De Quincey","gender":"M","genre":"Memoir","year":1839,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/42909/pg42909.txt","reason":"Contains De Quincey's famous 'Recollections of the Lakes and the Lake Poets', essential for Lakeland literary history."}
{"title":"Memoirs of William Wordsworth","author":"January Searle","gender":"M","genre":"Biography","year":1852,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/72281/pg72281.txt","reason":"A mid-nineteenth-century biography heavily detailing Wordsworth's life and environment in the Lake District."}
{"title":"Wordsworth's Poetical Works, Volume 1","author":"William Wordsworth","gender":"M","genre":"Poetry","year":1882,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/10219/pg10219.txt","reason":"Contains early poems and numerous topographical references to the Lake District environment."}
{"title":"Wordsworth's Poetical Works, Volume 2","author":"William Wordsworth","gender":"M","genre":"Poetry","year":1882,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/12145/pg12145.txt","reason":"Includes 'The Brothers' and 'Michael', both deeply rooted in the pastoral life of the Lake District."}
{"title":"Wordsworth's Poetical Works, Volume 3","author":"William Wordsworth","gender":"M","genre":"Poetry","year":1882,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/12383/pg12383.txt","reason":"Features the daffodils poem based on Ullswater and other central Lakeland verses."}
{"title":"Wordsworth's Poetical Works, Volume 4","author":"William Wordsworth","gender":"M","genre":"Poetry","year":1882,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/32459/pg32459.txt","reason":"Includes poems such as 'The Waggoner' which map the geography between Grasmere and Keswick."}
{"title":"Wordsworth's Poetical Works, Volume 7","author":"William Wordsworth","gender":"M","genre":"Poetry","year":1882,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/47143/pg47143.txt","reason":"Contains the River Duddon sonnets mapping the course of the famous Lake District river."}
{"title":"The Poetical Works of William Wordsworth (The Excursion)","author":"William Wordsworth","gender":"M","genre":"Poetry","year":1814,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/56361/pg56361.txt","reason":"A long philosophical poem set in the valleys and mountains of the Lake District, primarily Langdale."}
{"title":"The Prose Works of William Wordsworth","author":"William Wordsworth","gender":"M","genre":"Essay","year":1876,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/16550/pg16550.txt","reason":"Contains his famous 'Guide through the District of the Lakes', a seminal text in Lake District literature."}
{"title":"Journals of Dorothy Wordsworth Vol. I","author":"Dorothy Wordsworth","gender":"F","genre":"Diary","year":1897,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/42856/pg42856.txt","reason":"The Grasmere Journals provide daily observations of nature and life in the Lake District."}
{"title":"Letters of Samuel Taylor Coleridge, Vol. 1","author":"Samuel Taylor Coleridge","gender":"M","genre":"Letters","year":1895,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/44553/pg44553.txt","reason":"Includes Coleridge's letters describing his walks in the Lake District, including his descent of Scafell."}
{"title":"Specimens of the Table Talk of S.T. Coleridge","author":"Samuel Taylor Coleridge","gender":"M","genre":"Memoir","year":1835,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/8489/pg8489.txt","reason":"Reflections on literature and life, many stemming from his time as a Lake Poet at Greta Hall."}
{"title":"Biographia Epistolaris Vol. II","author":"Samuel Taylor Coleridge","gender":"M","genre":"Letters","year":1817,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/59226/pg59226.txt","reason":"Biographical letters detailing his relationships with other Lake Poets and his life in Keswick."}
{"title":"The Literary Remains of Samuel Taylor Coleridge, Volume 1","author":"Samuel Taylor Coleridge","gender":"M","genre":"Essay","year":1836,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/8488/pg8488.txt","reason":"Posthumous collections of notes, some originating from his Lake District notebooks."}
{"title":"The Complete Poetical Works of Samuel Taylor Coleridge Vol 1","author":"Samuel Taylor Coleridge","gender":"M","genre":"Poetry","year":1834,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/29090/pg29090.txt","reason":"Includes 'Christabel' and other poems written while living in and inspired by the Lake District."}
{"title":"The Complete Poetical Works of Samuel Taylor Coleridge Vol 2","author":"Samuel Taylor Coleridge","gender":"M","genre":"Poetry","year":1834,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/29092/pg29092.txt","reason":"Further poetry and dramatic works from the Lake Poet."}
{"title":"The Life of Samuel Taylor Coleridge","author":"James Gillman","gender":"M","genre":"Biography","year":1838,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/8957/pg8957.txt","reason":"Details Coleridge's time living in the Lake District and his interactions with Wordsworth and Southey."}
{"title":"Climbing in the British Isles - England","author":"W. P. Haskett Smith","gender":"M","genre":"Mountaineering","year":1894,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/37993/pg37993.txt","reason":"An early climbing guide with extensive, detailed chapters on ascents in the Lake District like Scafell and Pillar."}
{"title":"Early Reviews of English Poets","author":"John Louis Haney","gender":"M","genre":"Essay","year":1900,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/18766/pg18766.txt","reason":"Compiles the critical reception of the 'Lake School' of poetry during the 19th century."}
{"title":"Brief History of English and American Literature","author":"Henry A. Beers","gender":"M","genre":"History","year":1897,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/21090/pg21090.txt","reason":"Contains detailed sections analysing the Lake Poets and their connection to the landscape."}
{"title":"The Doctor, &c., Vol. 6","author":"Robert Southey","gender":"M","genre":"Fiction","year":1847,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/72540/pg72540.txt","reason":"Written by the Keswick-based Poet Laureate, full of regional Lake District observations and eccentricities."}
{"title":"Historic Sites of Lancashire and Cheshire","author":"James Croston","gender":"M","genre":"Topography","year":1883,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/45153/pg45153.txt","reason":"Explores the historical geography of the North West, including the Furness region of the Lake District."}
{"title":"Famous English Poets","author":"Various","gender":"M","genre":"Biography","year":1880,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/49805/pg49805.txt","reason":"Contains dedicated biographical chapters on the Lake Poets and their geographic inspirations."}
{"title":"Graham's Magazine, Vol. XLI","author":"Various","gender":"M","genre":"Literature","year":1852,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/47752/pg47752.txt","reason":"Contains 'Derwentwater', a literary piece romanticising the Lake District lake and its history."}
{"title":"Lakeland Words","author":"Bryham Kirkby","gender":"M","genre":"Linguistics","year":1898,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/58200/pg58200.txt","reason":"A glossary of dialect words and phrases used in Cumberland and Westmorland."}
{"title":"A Guide to the Lakes, in Cumberland, Westmorland, and Lancashire","author":"Thomas West","gender":"M","genre":"Guide","year":1778,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/aguidetothelake01westgoog/aguidetothelake01westgoog_djvu.txt","reason":"The first major picturesque guide to the Lake District, establishing the 'stations' for viewing the landscape."}
{"title":"Observations, relative chiefly to picturesque beauty, made in the year 1772, on several parts of England; particularly the mountains, and lakes of Cumberland, and Westmoreland","author":"William Gilpin","gender":"M","genre":"Travel","year":1786,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/observationsrel00gilpgoog/observationsrel00gilpgoog_djvu.txt","reason":"A foundational text of the Picturesque movement focused directly on the Lake District scenery."}
{"title":"A Survey of the Lakes of Cumberland, Westmorland, and Lancashire","author":"James Clarke","gender":"M","genre":"Topography","year":1787,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/surveyoflakesofc00clar/surveyoflakesofc00clar_djvu.txt","reason":"Early and highly detailed topographical and historical survey of the Lake District with maps."}
{"title":"A Fortnight's Ramble to the Lakes in Westmoreland, Lancashire, and Cumberland","author":"Joseph Budworth","gender":"M","genre":"Travel","year":1792,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/fortnightsramble00budw/fortnightsramble00budw_djvu.txt","reason":"One of the earliest published pedestrian tours of the Lake District."}
{"title":"An Excursion to the Lakes in Westmoreland and Cumberland","author":"William Hutchinson","gender":"M","genre":"Travel","year":1774,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/anexcursiontola00hutcgoog/anexcursiontola00hutcgoog_djvu.txt","reason":"An early antiquarian and scenic tour of the Lake District."}
{"title":"The Lake Country","author":"E. Lynn Linton","gender":"F","genre":"Topography","year":1864,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/lakecountry00lintgoog/lakecountry00lintgoog_djvu.txt","reason":"A comprehensive Victorian descriptive work of the Lake District written by a native of Keswick."}
{"title":"A Topographical Description of Cumberland, Westmoreland, Lancashire, and a Part of the North Riding of Yorkshire","author":"John Housman","gender":"M","genre":"Topography","year":1800,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/topographicaldes00hous/topographicaldes00hous_djvu.txt","reason":"Includes a highly detailed guidebook section specifically mapping out a tour of the Lakes."}
{"title":"A Complete Guide to the English Lakes","author":"Harriet Martineau","gender":"F","genre":"Guide","year":1855,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/completeguidetoe00mart/completeguidetoe00mart_djvu.txt","reason":"The definitive mid-Victorian guidebook to the Lake District, written by a prominent Ambleside resident."}
{"title":"A Concise Description of the English Lakes","author":"Jonathan Otley","gender":"M","genre":"Guide","year":1823,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/concisedescripti00otle/concisedescripti00otle_djvu.txt","reason":"The first accurate geological and geographical guide to the Lake District."}
{"title":"The Tourist's New Guide, containing a description of the Lakes, Mountains, and Scenery in Cumberland, Westmorland, and Lancashire","author":"William Green","gender":"M","genre":"Guide","year":1819,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/touristsnewguide00gree/touristsnewguide00gree_djvu.txt","reason":"A monumental two-volume artistic and descriptive guide to the Lake District by an Ambleside artist."}
{"title":"Geology of the Lake District","author":"Adam Sedgwick","gender":"M","genre":"Geology","year":1843,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/geologyoflakedis00sedg/geologyoflakedis00sedg_djvu.txt","reason":"A series of letters forming the foundational geological survey of the Lake District mountains."}
{"title":"Rambles in the Lake Country and its Borders","author":"Edwin Waugh","gender":"M","genre":"Travel","year":1861,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/ramblesinlakecou00waug/ramblesinlakecou00waug_djvu.txt","reason":"A Victorian travelogue detailing walking tours through the Cumbrian landscape."}
{"title":"Literary Associations of the English Lakes","author":"H. D. Rawnsley","gender":"M","genre":"Topography","year":1894,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/literaryassociat00rawn/literaryassociat00rawn_djvu.txt","reason":"Explores the locations in the Lake District connected to its famous writers and poets."}
{"title":"Life and Nature at the English Lakes","author":"H. D. Rawnsley","gender":"M","genre":"Nature","year":1899,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/lifeandnatureat00rawn/lifeandnatureat00rawn_djvu.txt","reason":"Essays on the ecology, customs, and conservation of the Lake District by the co-founder of the National Trust."}
{"title":"A Tour thro' the whole Island of Great Britain","author":"Daniel Defoe","gender":"M","genre":"Travel","year":1724,"repository":"Project Gutenberg","download_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/38080/pg38080.txt","reason":"Contains Defoe's famous early description of Westmorland and the Lake District as a 'barren and frightful' landscape."}
{"title":"Highways and Byways in the Lake District","author":"A. G. Bradley","gender":"M","genre":"Travel","year":1900,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/highwaysbywaysin00brad/highwaysbywaysin00brad_djvu.txt","reason":"A comprehensive travel narrative covering the culture and scenery of the Lake District at the turn of the century."}
{"title":"The English Lake District as Interpreted in the Poems of Wordsworth","author":"William Angus Knight","gender":"M","genre":"Topography","year":1878,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/englishlakedistr00knig/englishlakedistr00knig_djvu.txt","reason":"A detailed mapping of Wordsworth's poetry to specific geographic locations in the Lake District."}
{"title":"A Descriptive Poem, Addressed to Two Ladies, at their Return from Viewing the Mines near Whitehaven","author":"John Dalton","gender":"M","genre":"Poetry","year":1755,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/descriptivepoem00dalt/descriptivepoem00dalt_djvu.txt","reason":"One of the earliest poetic works to celebrate the sublime mountain scenery of the Lake District."}
{"title":"A Description of the Lake at Keswick","author":"John Brown","gender":"M","genre":"Letter","year":1767,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/descriptionoflak00brow/descriptionoflak00brow_djvu.txt","reason":"A famous early letter praising the perfection of Derwentwater, highly influential on early tourism."}
{"title":"A Journey Made in the Summer of 1794, through Holland and the Western Frontier of Germany, with a Return Down the Rhine; to which are added Observations during a Tour to the Lakes of Lancashire, Westmoreland, and Cumberland","author":"Ann Radcliffe","gender":"F","genre":"Travel","year":1795,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/journeymadeinsum00radc/journeymadeinsum00radc_djvu.txt","reason":"The Gothic novelist's influential account of the sublime and picturesque qualities of the Lake District."}
{"title":"The Minstrels of Winandermere","author":"Charles Farish","gender":"M","genre":"Poetry","year":1811,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/minstrelsofwinan00fari/minstrelsofwinan00fari_djvu.txt","reason":"A romantic poem set around Windermere, capturing local Cumbrian history and landscape."}
{"title":"Letters from the Lakes","author":"John Briggs","gender":"M","genre":"Travel","year":1825,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/lettersfromthel00brig/lettersfromthel00brig_djvu.txt","reason":"A series of descriptive letters exploring the landscape and rural character of the Lake District."}
{"title":"The Northmen in Cumberland and Westmoreland","author":"Robert Ferguson","gender":"M","genre":"History","year":1856,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/northmenincumber00ferg/northmenincumber00ferg_djvu.txt","reason":"An antiquarian study of Norse place-names and Viking heritage in the Lake District."}
{"title":"A History of Cumberland","author":"Richard S. Ferguson","gender":"M","genre":"History","year":1890,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/historyofcumberl00ferg/historyofcumberl00ferg_djvu.txt","reason":"A comprehensive county history containing substantial material on the northern Lake District."}
{"title":"A History of Westmorland","author":"Richard S. Ferguson","gender":"M","genre":"History","year":1894,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/historyofwestmor00ferg/historyofwestmor00ferg_djvu.txt","reason":"A comprehensive county history containing substantial material on the southern Lake District."}
{"title":"Hawkshead: its History, Archaeology, Industries, Folklore, Dialect","author":"Henry Swainson Cowper","gender":"M","genre":"History","year":1899,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/hawksheaditshist00cowp/hawksheaditshist00cowp_djvu.txt","reason":"An exhaustive local history of one of the most prominent market towns in the Lake District."}
{"title":"Geological Fragments collected principally from rambles among the rocks of Furness and Cartmel","author":"John Bolton","gender":"M","genre":"Geology","year":1869,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/geologicalfragme00bolt/geologicalfragme00bolt_djvu.txt","reason":"A local geologist's account of the southern fringes of the Lake District."}
{"title":"Ballads in the Cumberland Dialect","author":"Robert Anderson","gender":"M","genre":"Poetry","year":1805,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/balladsincumberl00ande/balladsincumberl00ande_djvu.txt","reason":"Classic Cumbrian dialect poetry reflecting the rural culture of the Lake District and its surroundings."}
{"title":"The Geology of the Northern Part of the English Lake District","author":"J. Clifton Ward","gender":"M","genre":"Geology","year":1876,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/geologyofnorthe00ward/geologyofnorthe00ward_djvu.txt","reason":"An official Geological Survey memoir detailing the volcanic rocks of the northern Lakes."}
{"title":"Miscellaneous Poems","author":"Ewan Clark","gender":"M","genre":"Poetry","year":1779,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/miscellaneouspoe00clar/miscellaneouspoe00clar_djvu.txt","reason":"Contains several regional poems celebrating Cumberland life and scenery."}
{"title":"Desultory Thoughts in London, Titus and Gisippus, with other Poems","author":"Charles Lloyd","gender":"M","genre":"Poetry","year":1821,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/desultorythought00lloy/desultorythought00lloy_djvu.txt","reason":"Poems by a member of the Lake School who lived at Old Brathay near Ambleside."}
{"title":"Tours to the British Mountains","author":"Thomas Wilkinson","gender":"M","genre":"Travel","year":1824,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/tourstobritishmo00wilk/tourstobritishmo00wilk_djvu.txt","reason":"Written by Wordsworth's Quaker friend from Yanwath, describing early walks over the Lake District fells."}
{"title":"A Companion and Useful Guide to the Beauties of Scotland, and the Hebrides, to the Lakes of Westmoreland, Cumberland, and Lancashire","author":"Sarah Murray","gender":"F","genre":"Guide","year":1799,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/companionandusef00murr/companionandusef00murr_djvu.txt","reason":"An early and highly practical travel guide to the Lake District written by a pioneering female tourist."}
{"title":"The Lakes in Sunshine","author":"James Payn","gender":"M","genre":"Topography","year":1867,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/lakesinsunshine00payn/lakesinsunshine00payn_djvu.txt","reason":"A Victorian photographic and descriptive book celebrating the beauty of the Lake District."}
{"title":"Night and the Soul","author":"John Stanyan Bigg","gender":"M","genre":"Poetry","year":1854,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/nightandsoulpoem00bigg/nightandsoulpoem00bigg_djvu.txt","reason":"A Spasmodic poem written by a native of Ulverston, heavily imbued with Lake District imagery."}
{"title":"The Poetical Works of Miss Susanna Blamire, 'The Muse of Cumberland'","author":"Susanna Blamire","gender":"F","genre":"Poetry","year":1842,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/poeticalworksofm00blam/poeticalworksofm00blam_djvu.txt","reason":"Posthumous collection of poems and songs deeply rooted in Cumbrian culture and dialect."}
{"title":"Cummerland Talk","author":"John Richardson","gender":"M","genre":"Fiction","year":1871,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/cummerlandtalk00rich/cummerlandtalk00rich_djvu.txt","reason":"Tales and rhymes in the Cumbrian dialect capturing the mid-Victorian rural life of the Lake District."}
{"title":"A Tour in Scotland, 1769","author":"Thomas Pennant","gender":"M","genre":"Travel","year":1771,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/tourinscotland1700penn/tourinscotland1700penn_djvu.txt","reason":"Contains a highly influential early description of the Lake District on his route north."}
{"title":"Letters to the Young","author":"Maria Jane Jewsbury","gender":"F","genre":"Letters","year":1828,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/letterstoyoung00jews/letterstoyoung00jews_djvu.txt","reason":"Written by a friend of Wordsworth, containing reflections inspired by her visits to the Lake District."}
{"title":"A Family Tour through the British Empire","author":"Priscilla Wakefield","gender":"F","genre":"Travel","year":1804,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/familytourthroug00wake/familytourthroug00wake_djvu.txt","reason":"An educational travelogue containing a substantial descriptive section on the Lake District."}
{"title":"The River Duddon, a Series of Sonnets","author":"William Wordsworth","gender":"M","genre":"Poetry","year":1820,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/riverduddonserie00word/riverduddonserie00word_djvu.txt","reason":"A sonnet sequence tracking the course of the Duddon from the fells to the sea, with topographical notes."}
{"title":"Thorstein of the Mere; a Saga of the Northmen in Lakeland","author":"William G. Collingwood","gender":"M","genre":"Fiction","year":1895,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/thorsteinoftheme00coll/thorsteinoftheme00coll_djvu.txt","reason":"A historical novel set in the Lake District, exploring its Norse history and geography."}
{"title":"The Bondwomen: A Saga of Langdale","author":"William G. Collingwood","gender":"M","genre":"Fiction","year":1896,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/bondwomensagaofl00coll/bondwomensagaofl00coll_djvu.txt","reason":"A late-Victorian novel deeply immersed in the Viking heritage and landscape of Langdale in the Lake District."}
{"title":"Papers, Letters, and Journals of William Pearson","author":"William Pearson","gender":"M","genre":"Memoir","year":1863,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/paperslettersjou00pear/paperslettersjou00pear_djvu.txt","reason":"Writings of a Westmorland naturalist and friend of Wordsworth, recording the ecology of the Lake District borders."}
{"title":"A Description of Scenery in the Lake District","author":"William Ford","gender":"M","genre":"Guide","year":1840,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/descriptionofsce00ford/descriptionofsce00ford_djvu.txt","reason":"An itinerary and guidebook intended for tourists exploring the central Lake District."}
{"title":"Manners and Customs of Westmorland","author":"John Gough","gender":"M","genre":"History","year":1827,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/mannersandcustom00goug/mannersandcustom00goug_djvu.txt","reason":"An antiquarian account of the rural traditions, speech, and lifestyle of the Lake District population."}
{"title":"An Essay towards a Natural History of Westmorland and Cumberland","author":"Thomas Robinson","gender":"M","genre":"Natural History","year":1709,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/essaytowardsnatu00robi/essaytowardsnatu00robi_djvu.txt","reason":"An early modern attempt to categorise the geology, flora, and fauna of the Lake District."}
{"title":"Cumberland and Westmoreland, Ancient and Modern","author":"John Sullivan","gender":"M","genre":"History","year":1857,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/cumberlandwestmo00sull/cumberlandwestmo00sull_djvu.txt","reason":"An exploration of the Celtic and Norse antiquities, dialects, and place-names of the Lake District."}
{"title":"The Folk-Speech of Cumberland","author":"Alexander Craig Gibson","gender":"M","genre":"Linguistics","year":1869,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/folkspeechofcumb00gibs/folkspeechofcumb00gibs_djvu.txt","reason":"A study and collection of dialect texts capturing the regional culture of the Lake District."}
{"title":"Leaves from Lakeland","author":"James Payn","gender":"M","genre":"Essay","year":1858,"repository":"Internet Archive","download_url":"https://archive.org/download/leavesfromlakela00payn/leavesfromlakela00payn_djvu.txt","reason":"A collection of picturesque and narrative sketches based on the author's residence in the Lake District."}
